      "text": "Human mastery could change the quality of the questions a builder asks. A practised player may recognise a useful observation sooner, retire a false theory before it burns the budget, or notice that a plan has drifted from what is actually on the board. The interesting unknown is which of those judgments Peter has made explicit in his agent—and which proved difficult to transfer. That is where a detailed account of his work could teach us something.",
